I have heard of two kinds of whetstone: the oil-stone and the water-stone.
I have no idea what the detailed difference is, but I have noticed that the
fine-grit stones sold retail work well with oil on them, and the large,
wheel-shaped stones used by farmers, for instance, are often wetted with
water.  I have now exhaused my expertise about whet-craft as well as wet-craft,
and appeal to those who actually know something.

I have a feeling that an experienced fighter, having some leisure and a
dull weapon, might rub it against anything suitably hard in order to improve
the edge.  He might have preferences, but will not ignore the need to
attend to his gear no matter that the ideal tool is missing.  


